<title>USA: J.P.Morgan names pair to board.</title>
<headline>J.P.Morgan names pair to board.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>J.P. Morgan &amp; Co Inc said Thursday it named Paul Allaire, chairman and chief executive of Xerox Corp, and Ellen Futter, president of the American Museum of Natural History to its board of directors.</p>
<p>Their elections become effective September 1.</p>
<p>Allaire is also a director of Sara Lee Corp, the New York Stock Exchange, SmithKline Beecham PLC and Lucent Technologies Inc.</p>
<p>Futter is on the board of Bristol-Myers Squibb Co and Consolidated Edison Co of New York Inc.</p>
